Article 42. Engaging in drug production activities shall meet the following conditions:
(1) Having pharmaceutical technical personnel, engineering technical personnel and corresponding technical workers who have been qualified according to law;
(2) Having premises, facilities and sanitary environment suitable for drug production;
(3) Having institutions and personnel capable of quality management and quality inspection of the drugs produced, as well as necessary instruments and equipment;
(4) Having rules and regulations to ensure drug quality, and complying with the requirements of the Good Manufacturing Practice for drugs formulated by the drug regulatory department of the State Council pursuant to this Law.

Article 52. Engaging in drug distribution activities shall meet the following conditions:
(1) Having pharmacists or other pharmaceutical technical personnel who have been qualified according to law;
(2) Having business premises, equipment, storage facilities and sanitary environment suitable for the drugs distributed;
(3) Having a quality management institution or personnel suitable for the drugs distributed;
(4) Having rules and regulations to ensure drug quality, and complying with the requirements of the Good Supply Practice for drugs formulated by the drug regulatory department of the State Council pursuant to this Law.

Article 98 It is prohibited to produce (including compounding, hereinafter the same), distribute, or use counterfeit drugs or substandard drugs.
Any of the following circumstances constitutes a counterfeit drug:
(1) the ingredients contained in the drug are inconsistent with the ingredients specified in the national drug standards;
(2) a non-drug substance is passed off as a drug, or one drug is passed off as another drug;
(3) the drug is deteriorated;
(4) the indications or functions indicated on the drug exceed the specified scope.
Any of the following circumstances constitutes a substandard drug:
(1) the content of the active ingredients in the drug does not meet the national drug standards;
(2) the drug is contaminated;
(3) the drug has no labeled expiry date or the expiry date has been altered;
(4) the drug has no indicated batch number or the batch number has been altered;
(5) the drug has exceeded its expiry date;
(6) the drug has been added with preservatives or excipients without authorization;
(7) other drugs that do not meet the drug standards.
It is prohibited to produce or import drugs without obtaining a drug approval certificate; it is prohibited to produce drugs using active pharmaceutical ingredients, packaging materials, and containers that have not undergone review and approval in accordance with regulations.

Article 124 Whoever violates the provisions of this Law and commits any of the following acts shall confiscate the illegally manufactured, imported, or sold drugs and illegal gains, as well as raw materials, excipients, packaging materials and production equipment specially used for illegal production, order suspension of production or business for rectification, and impose a fine of not less than fifteen times but not more than thirty times the value of the illegally manufactured, imported, or sold drugs; if the value is less than 100,000 yuan, it shall be calculated as 100,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, shall revoke the drug approval certificate document, and even revoke the drug manufacturing permit, drug business permit or medical institution preparation permit, and for the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other responsible persons, shall confiscate the income obtained from the unit during the period of the illegal act, and impose a fine of not less than thirty percent but not more than three times the income obtained, and shall prohibit them from engaging in drug manufacturing and business activities for ten years up to life, and may also impose detention of not less than five days but not more than fifteen days by the public security organ:
(1) Manufacturing or importing drugs without a drug approval certificate document;
(2) Manufacturing or importing drugs using a drug approval certificate document obtained by fraudulent means;
(3) Manufacturing drugs using active pharmaceutical ingredients that have not undergone evaluation and approval;
(4) Selling drugs that should have been inspected but were not inspected;
(5) Manufacturing or selling drugs whose use is prohibited by the drug regulatory department of the State Council;
(6) Falsifying manufacturing or inspection records;
(7) Making major changes in the drug manufacturing process without approval.
Whoever sells the drugs specified in items (1) to (3) of the preceding paragraph, or a drug use unit uses the drugs specified in items (1) to (5) of the preceding paragraph, shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph; if the circumstances are serious, and the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other responsible persons of the drug use unit have a practice certificate for medical and health personnel, the practice certificate shall also be revoked.
Where a small quantity of drugs that have been legally marketed abroad is imported without approval, if the circumstances are minor, the punishment may be mitigated or exempted according to law.

Article 125 Whoever violates the provisions of this Law and commits any of the following acts shall confiscate the illegally manufactured or sold drugs and illegal gains, as well as packaging materials and containers, order suspension of production or business for rectification, and impose a fine of not less than 500,000 yuan but not more than 5,000,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, shall revoke the drug approval certificate document, drug manufacturing permit, and drug business permit, and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan on the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other responsible persons, and shall prohibit them from engaging in drug manufacturing and business activities for ten years up to life:
(1) Carrying out a clinical trial of a drug without approval;
(2) Manufacturing drugs using packaging materials or containers that have not undergone evaluation and directly contact the drugs, or selling such drugs;
(3) Using labels or package inserts that have not been approved.

Article 127 Whoever violates the provisions of this Law and commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections within a prescribed time limit and given a warning; if it fails to make corrections within the time limit, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) Carrying out a bioequivalence test without filing;
(2) During a drug clinical trial, upon discovery of safety issues or other risks, the clinical trial sponsor fails to timely adjust the clinical trial protocol, suspend or terminate the clinical trial, or fails to report to the drug regulatory department of the State Council;
(3) Failing to establish and implement a drug traceability system in accordance with regulations;
(4) Failing to submit an annual report in accordance with regulations;
(5) Failing to file or report changes in the drug manufacturing process in accordance with regulations;
(6) Failing to formulate a post-marketing risk management plan for the drug;
(7) Failing to carry out post-marketing research or post-marketing evaluation of the drug in accordance with regulations.

Article 137 Whoever commits any of the following acts shall be given a severe punishment within the range of punishment provided for in this Law:
(1) Passing off narcotic drugs, psychotropic substances, medicinal toxic drugs, radioactive drugs, or drug-like precursor chemicals as other drugs, or passing off other drugs as the aforesaid drugs;
(2) Manufacturing or selling counterfeit drugs or inferior drugs mainly for use by pregnant women, parturients, or children;
(3) The biological products manufactured or sold are counterfeit drugs or inferior drugs;
(4) Manufacturing or selling counterfeit drugs or inferior drugs, causing personal injury;
(5) Reoffending after being punished for manufacturing or selling counterfeit drugs or inferior drugs;
(6) Refusing or evading supervision and inspection, forging, destroying, or concealing relevant evidentiary materials, or using sealed or seized articles without authorization.

Article 147 Where a drug regulatory authority violates the provisions of this Law by committing any of the following acts, the relevant license shall be revoked, and the directly responsible manager and other directly liable persons shall be given disciplinary sanctions according to law:
(1) approving a drug clinical trial when the conditions are not met;
(2) issuing a drug registration certificate for a drug that does not meet the conditions;
(3) issuing a drug manufacturing license, drug distribution license, or medical institution preparation license to an entity that does not meet the conditions.

Article 148 Where a local people's government at or above the county level violates the provisions of this Law by committing any of the following acts, the directly responsible manager and other directly liable persons shall be given a demerit or major demerit; if the circumstances are serious, they shall be given demotion, removal from office, or expulsion:
(1) concealing, falsely reporting, delaying reporting, or omitting reporting a drug safety incident;
(2) failing to timely eliminate major regional drug safety hazards, resulting in an extremely serious drug safety incident within its administrative region, or consecutive serious drug safety incidents;
(3) failing to perform its duties effectively, causing serious adverse effects or significant losses.

Article 149 Where a drug regulatory authority or other relevant department violates the provisions of this Law by committing any of the following acts, the directly responsible manager and other directly liable persons shall be given a demerit or major demerit; if the circumstances are relatively serious, they shall be given demotion or removal from office; if the circumstances are serious, they shall be given expulsion:
(1) concealing, falsely reporting, delaying reporting, or omitting reporting a drug safety incident;
(2) failing to promptly investigate and punish discovered drug safety violations;
(3) failing to timely discover systemic drug safety risks, or failing to timely eliminate drug safety hazards within the area under its supervision and management, causing serious impact;
(4) other failures to perform drug supervision and management duties, causing serious adverse effects or significant losses.
